name: YouTube Analytics
command: "{{INSTALL_PATH}}/mcp_servers/youtube_analytics{{EXECUTABLE_EXT}}"
shortDescription: Analyze your own YouTube channels
description: >-
  Analytics for YouTube channels you own via Google's official APIs: channel health vs the
  previous period, per-video performance, audience retention and drop-off points, thumbnail
  impressions and click-through rate, traffic sources and search terms, audience demographics,
  trends and comments. Uses your own Google Cloud OAuth client (Desktop app).
type: built-in
secret_keys:
  - YOUTUBE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID
  - YOUTUBE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
instructions: >-
  Start with list_channels; if nothing is connected, call connect_channel, which opens Google
  sign-in in the browser. YouTube Analytics data lags 2-3 days, so rolling periods end 3 days ago;
  say so when the user asks about very recent uploads. Impressions and CTR come from daily reach
  reports that start about 48 hours after a channel is connected and include the prior 30 days;
  relay the coverage note instead of guessing. For "why did this video underperform", use
  video_report first, then video_retention for exact drop-off timestamps. Always name the period
  you are describing.
